# Template for your personal client list. bin/setup-guards copies it to .client-terms
# (gitignored, chmod 600). Put the real names in .client-terms, never in this file.
#
# Every organization you consult for goes in .client-terms, one entry per line.
# tools/org_audit.py blocks them in commits, pushes and Claude edits.
#
# Plain entries match regardless of case, extra spaces, hyphens, underscores, dots,
# line wraps or no space at all. "Example Clearing" also catches "EXAMPLE  CLEARING",
# "example-clearing", "ExampleClearing" and "exampleclearing.com". CamelCase splits
# into words.
# Regex entries: prefix with re: or wrap in slashes. Regex is case-insensitive.
#
# Add short forms and internal domains too. A client named only by a bare word with
# no company suffix ("Meridian runs three clusters") is caught ONLY if it is listed here.
#
# Examples (delete these and add your own in .client-terms):
# Example Clearing
# EXCL
# re:\bexcl-?corp\.internal\b
# /prd-kafka-\d+\.example\.net/
